      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "e5c269fd-ead8-50e4-b16e-9d9e9b4a244c",
        ":question/problem": "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=1-4y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x & =1-4y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x \\\\ 2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x & =1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)}_{\u23df}}_{P(x)}y & ={{\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}}_{\u23df}}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "ef647b19-79e2-5b54-b8df-1bf5fe9db9b4",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "c4bcf009-6fca-5110-8ae8-643678b3cb9e"
            ],
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "f4a26a57-987c-5668-b531-e2f3db2b75bc",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)y=1+\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "c4bcf009-6fca-5110-8ae8-643678b3cb9e",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)y=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "b6972414-a235-5987-855e-567ba571b605",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)y=1+3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "eb82a4b2-58af-556c-a366-f92624768704",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)y=1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "e08cc03c-cea4-583d-b68b-e5c8622f76e1",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x}{2}=(2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)y"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
